     The computer BIOS starts in text mode, and the FreeBSD loader(8) runs,
     loading the kernel.  If _h_w_._v_g_a_._t_e_x_t_m_o_d_e is set, the system remains in
     text mode.  Otherwise, vvtt switches to 640x480x16 VGA mode using vvtt__vvggaa.
     If a KMS (Kernel Mode Setting) video driver is available, the display is
     switched to high resolution and the KMS driver takes over.  When a KMS
     driver is not available, vvtt__vvggaa remains active.

